AiTask qa5_t01_big_orders {
  label: 'QA5 T01 Big Orders'
  description: 'Checks @Dataset:ecommerce_official for orders over $1,000 placed yesterday and emails nhi.ty@holistics.io only when qualifying orders exist.'

  brief: @md
    Using @Dataset:ecommerce_official, query fresh data for orders placed during the full calendar day immediately preceding the task run date, using the workspace timezone.

    Calculate each order's value as the sum of its order-item quantities multiplied by product prices. Return only orders with an order value strictly greater than **$1,000**.

    If one or more qualifying orders exist, send a concise, scannable email through the available AI delivery capability to **nhi.ty@holistics.io**. The subject must begin exactly with **[QA5 T01]** and identify that the message contains yesterday's large orders. Include the reporting date and a row for every qualifying order with:
    - Order ID
    - Status
    - Order value, formatted as USD

    If there are no qualifying orders, do not send an email or any other delivery. Do not infer causes or include unsupported claims.
  ;;

  acceptance_criteria: @md
    - The analysis runs a fresh query against @Dataset:ecommerce_official and covers exactly the full calendar day immediately preceding the task run date in the workspace timezone.
    - Each order's value is accurately calculated as the sum of order-item quantity multiplied by product price.
    - Only orders with value strictly greater than $1,000 are included.
    - When qualifying orders exist, exactly one concise email is delivered to nhi.ty@holistics.io; its subject begins exactly with [QA5 T01] and it lists every qualifying order's ID, status, and USD-formatted order value.
    - When no qualifying orders exist, no email or other delivery is sent.
    - All reported values and statements are grounded in the fresh query results, with no invented data or unsupported claims.
  ;;
}